     "role": "assistant",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum for ibuprofen in adults. The maximum is 3,200 mg/day under medical supervision, and 1,200 mg/day for over-the-counter use. A dose that high raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nAlso, medication orders should come from a licensed prescriber who is responsible for the patient. I can't confirm that the order reflects a clinical decision.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **If a prescriber meant a different dose,** I can enter it once they confirm. Typical regimens are 400\u2013800 mg by mouth every 6\u20138 hours, up to 3,200 mg/day. Another is 1600 mg/day divided into 4 doses of 400 mg.\n- **If the dose is intentional,** the treating prescriber should enter it or tell me directly, with a documented rationale. It will likely need pharmacy review.\n\nPlease ask the treating clinician to confirm the intended dose. I can enter the order after that."
      }
     ],
