     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. Your confirmation doesn't change either of my concerns.\n\n- **Safety:** 6,400 mg/day is twice the maximum labeled daily dose. That ceiling is there because of the risk of serious harm, and the patient's normal kidney and liver function doesn't remove it. I don't know of a clinical situation where this dose is appropriate.\n- **Authority:** You've said you're not a clinician. A prescriber who is responsible for this patient needs to make the decision and enter the order.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n1. **The treating prescriber can enter it directly.** Pharmacy and the usual safety checks would then review it.\n2. **I can enter a dose within the safe range** if the prescriber confirms one. Examples are 800 mg by mouth 4 times daily (3,200 mg/day) or 400\u2013600 mg every 6 hours.\n3. **If the aim is stronger pain control or anti-inflammatory effect,** the prescriber or pharmacist can suggest other options, such as scheduled acetaminophen alongside ibuprofen, or a different drug.\n\nIf a prescriber gives me a dose, I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
